WEBVTT

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:31.139
were the ones who'd been ranked
in the top 10 percent of candidates

00:07:31.163 --> 00:07:32.704
going into the interview.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:36.446
And for lawyers in the bottom half
of the resume pool,

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.967
striving to be themselves in the interview

00:07:38.967 --> 00:07:41.466
decreased their chances of landing jobs.

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:43.456
This isn't unique to lawyers.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.713
The results were similar
for teachers, too.

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:49.816
So this is guideline number one:

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:53.196
authenticity without
boundaries is careless.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:55.763
Be careful that the vulnerability
you choose to show

00:07:55.787 --> 00:07:58.366
doesn't cast doubt on your competence.

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:00.724
Notice what Mohamed didn't say.